<header class="page-header">
    <h1>{{ title }}</h1>
    <p>A standalone PHP framework that keeps each page’s controller, model, and view together.</p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-sm mt-md">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="{{ url frameworkUrl }}">Build your first page</a>
        <a class="btn btn-outline" href="{{ url classesUrl }}">Look up a class</a>
    </div>
</header>
<section aria-labelledby="learning-path">
    <h2 id="learning-path">Build an application</h2>
    <ol class="docs-steps">
        <li><a href="{{ url frameworkUrl }}">Start the local server and build a page.</a> Follow a GET request from the URL through a controller and model to the HTML response.</li>
        <li><a href="{{ url templatesUrl }}">Create a shared layout.</a> Pass data into a template, render a list, and see how escaping works.</li>
        <li><a href="{{ url servicesUrl }}">Handle forms and store data.</a> Save a preference, protect a route with middleware, and try a database transaction.</li>
        <li><a href="{{ url apiGuideUrl }}">Create a JSON endpoint.</a> Send requests and compare successful and invalid responses.</li>
    </ol>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="docs-reference">
    <h2 id="docs-reference">Reference and styling</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-auto gap-md">
    {% for guide in guides %}
    <article class="card card-body">
        <h2><a href="{{ url guide.url }}">{{ guide.title }}</a></h2>
        <p>{{ guide.description }}</p>
    </article>
    {% endfor %}
    </div>
</section>
